{"page":38,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.05257,"w":0.19833,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"24 Chapter 1: Functions"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.093,"w":0.4139,"h":0.01375,"fs":0.01375,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Periodicity and Graphs of the Trigonometric Functions"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.11698,"w":0.59301,"h":0.07486,"fs":0.01279,"n":6,"k":1,"t":"When an angle of measure u and an angle of measure u + 2p are in standard position, their terminal rays coincide. The two angles therefore have the same trigonometric func- tion values: sin(u + 2p) = sin u, tan(u + 2p) = tan u, and so on. Similarly, cos(u - 2p) = cos u, sin(u - 2p) = sin u, and so on. We describe this repeating behav- ior by saying that the six basic trigonometric functions are periodic."},{"x":0.0592,"y":0.20062,"w":0.22451,"h":0.04095,"fs":0.01151,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"Periods of Trigonometric Functions Period P: tan(x + p) = tan x cot(x + p) = cot x"},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.22586,"w":0.53247,"h":0.02882,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"DEFINITION A function ƒ(x) is periodic if there is a positive number p such that ƒ(x + p) = ƒ(x) for every value of x. The smallest such value of p is the period of ƒ."},{"x":0.0592,"y":0.24734,"w":0.8572,"h":0.11058,"fs":0.01279,"n":10,"k":1,"t":"Period 2P: sin(x + 2p) = sin x cos(x + 2p) = cos x sec(x + 2p) = sec x csc(x + 2p) = csc x When we graph trigonometric functions in the coordinate plane, we usually denote the independent variable by x instead of u. Figure 1.44 shows that the tangent and cotangent functions have period p = p, and the other four functions have period 2p. Also, the sym- metries in these graphs reveal that the cosine and secant functions are even and the other four functions are odd (although this does not prove those results)."},{"x":0.82895,"y":0.38938,"w":0.0435,"h":0.0097,"fs":0.00921,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"y = tan x"},{"x":0.38665,"y":0.39681,"w":0.20743,"h":0.00921,"fs":0.00921,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"y y"},{"x":0.11556,"y":0.40343,"w":0.03529,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Even"},{"x":0.41144,"y":0.41299,"w":0.04481,"h":0.0097,"fs":0.00921,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"y = cos x"},{"x":0.64238,"y":0.41299,"w":0.04285,"h":0.0097,"fs":0.00921,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"y = sin x"},{"x":0.11638,"y":0.42963,"w":0.11075,"h":0.03138,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"cos(-x) = cos x sec(-x) = sec x"},{"x":0.73557,"y":0.43942,"w":0.06077,"h":0.01996,"fs":0.00921,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"3p 2 − −p−p"},{"x":0.78927,"y":0.43942,"w":0.08878,"h":0.01998,"fs":0.00921,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"2 0 p 2 p 3p"},{"x":0.50514,"y":0.44349,"w":0.20743,"h":0.00921,"fs":0.00921,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"x x"},{"x":0.32414,"y":0.45033,"w":0.17587,"h":0.01406,"fs":0.00921,"n":5,"k":0,"t":"0 −p p 2p −p"},{"x":0.41298,"y":0.45033,"w":0.28908,"h":0.01998,"fs":0.00921,"n":8,"k":0,"t":"2 3p 2 0 −p p 2p −p"},{"x":0.35935,"y":0.45036,"w":0.06069,"h":0.01994,"fs":0.00921,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"2 p"},{"x":0.5614,"y":0.45036,"w":0.05924,"h":0.01994,"fs":0.00921,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"2 p"},{"x":0.61357,"y":0.45036,"w":0.06341,"h":0.01995,"fs":0.00921,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"2 3p 2"},{"x":0.73276,"y":0.48091,"w":0.14191,"h":0.01995,"fs":0.00921,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"2 3p 2 Domain: x ≠± , ± , . . ."},{"x":0.33112,"y":0.4853,"w":0.10633,"h":0.0318,"fs":0.00921,"n":5,"k":0,"t":"Domain: −∞< x < ∞ Range: −1 ≤y ≤1 Period: 2p"},{"x":0.53333,"y":0.4853,"w":0.10633,"h":0.0318,"fs":0.00921,"n":5,"k":0,"t":"Domain: −∞< x < ∞ Range: −1 ≤y ≤1 Period: 2p"},{"x":0.11556,"y":0.50012,"w":0.03092,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Odd"},{"x":0.73232,"y":0.50198,"w":0.10736,"h":0.02075,"fs":0.00921,"n":4,"k":0,"t":"Range: −∞ < y < ∞ Period: p"},{"x":0.41187,"y":0.51745,"w":0.4102,"h":0.00921,"fs":0.00921,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"(a) (b) (c)"},{"x":0.11638,"y":0.52631,"w":0.12015,"h":0.06719,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"sin(-x) = -sin x tan(-x) = -tan x csc(-x) = -csc x cot(-x) = -cot x"},{"x":0.58527,"y":0.53355,"w":0.20989,"h":0.00921,"fs":0.00921,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"y y"},{"x":0.42628,"y":0.54015,"w":0.44787,"h":0.01174,"fs":0.00921,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"y = sec x 