os u, sin u) x2 + y2 = 1"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.76707,"w":0.593,"h":0.0435,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"The coordinates of any point P(x, y) in the plane can be expressed in terms of the point’s distance r from the origin and the angle u that ray OP makes with the positive x-axis (Fig- ure 1.40). Since x>r = cos u and y>r = sin u, we have"},{"x":0.07666,"y":0.79603,"w":0.03005,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"0 sin u 0"},{"x":0.52538,"y":0.82012,"w":0.18524,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"x = rcos u, y = rsin u."},{"x":0.11075,"y":0.8278,"w":0.03224,"h":0.01078,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"0 cos u 0"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.84314,"w":0.5931,"h":0.02882,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"When r = 1 we can apply the Pythagorean theorem to the reference right triangle in Figure 1.45 and obtain the equation"},{"x":0.55039,"y":0.90253,"w":0.3316,"h":0.01795,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"cos2 u + sin2 u = 1. (3)"},{"x":0.04849,"y":0.90787,"w":0.18806,"h":0.02763,"fs":0.01151,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"FIGURE 1.45 The reference triangle for a general angle u."}]}